  '77777777-7777-4777-8777-777777777777',
  'blog',
  'what-to-order-first-turkish-meal',
  'What to Order for Your First Turkish Meal',
  'A practical way to build a first Turkish meal with meze, bread, grilled dishes, vegetables, dessert, coffee and tea.',
  '[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A first Turkish meal is easiest to understand as a table that develops in layers. Instead of choosing one isolated entree, begin with contrasting small plates, add bread, select a warm dish or something from the grill, and leave room for dessert or coffee. The result can be as quick or as leisurely as the occasion requires.</p><h2>Begin with a few contrasting meze</h2><p>Meze are small dishes intended to be shared. A useful starting combination includes something creamy, something bright or spicy, and a vegetable preparation. Yogurt, chickpeas, eggplant, peppers, herbs, olive oil and lemon appear in many Turkish meze traditions. The contrast matters more than ordering a long list.</p><p>Use bread to move between flavors, but pace the table. Two or three meze can introduce the meal without crowding out the warm dishes that follow. Review the <a href=\"/menu\">current Turquaz menu</a> because dishes and availability can change.</p><h2>Add warmth from the oven or grill</h2><p>Pide, kebabs, kofte and vegetable plates create a natural second stage. Pide is a boat-shaped flatbread with a crisp edge and a tender center. Kebab describes a family of preparations rather than one recipe, while kofte generally refers to seasoned meat shaped for cooking. A mixed table can pair one substantial warm dish with vegetables, grains or salad.</p><h3>Order for the whole table</h3><p>Ask what everyone enjoys before ordering. A party that wants to explore can share several items, while a guest with a specific preference may want an individual plate. Ingredient and dietary questions should always be confirmed directly with the restaurant because recipes and kitchen practices can change.</p><h2>Finish with sweetness and a hot drink</h2><p>Baklava or another pastry brings texture and sweetness after savory food. Turkish coffee is concentrated and served in a small cup; Turkish tea is lighter and can extend the conversation. Neither needs to be rushed.</p><h2>A simple first-order plan</h2><ol><li>Choose two or three contrasting meze.</li><li>Add bread or a baked specialty.</li><li>Select a grilled, vegetable or grain-based main dish.</li><li>Share dessert if the table still has room.</li><li>End with Turkish tea or coffee.</li></ol><p>There is no single correct first order. The best introduction fits the people at the table. <a href=\"/#reservation\">Reserve a table at Turquaz</a> and use the live menu to plan the meal around current choices.</p>"}]',
  'published',
  'First Turkish Meal: What to Order | Turquaz SF',
  'Plan your first Turkish meal with meze, pide, grilled dishes, dessert, coffee and tea at Turquaz in San Francisco.',
